{"id":"word-break","title":"Word break","difficulty":"medium","pattern":"prefix reachability","statement":"<p>Return whether s can be split into a sequence of dictionary words (reusable).</p>","entry":{"python":"word_break","cpp":{"name":"wordBreak","ret":"bool","params":[["string","s"],["vector<string>","words"]]}},"kind":"function","compare":"exact","time_limit_ms":2000,"hints":["dp[i] = can the first i characters be split?","dp[i] is true if some word ends at i and dp[i \u2212 len(word)] is true. Only try lengths up to the longest word."],"complexity":"O(n \u00d7 L) set lookups (L = longest word)","starter":{"python":"def word_break(s, words):\n    pass\n","cpp":"bool wordBreak(string s, vector<string>& words) {\n    \n}\n"},"tests":[{"args":["leetcode",["leet","code"]],"expected":true,"sample":true},{"args":["applepenapple",["apple","pen"]],"expected":true,"sample":true},{"args":["catsandog",["cats","dog","sand","and","cat"]],"expected":false},{"args":["aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaab",["a","aa","aaa","aaaa"]],"expected":false},{"args":["",["a","aa","ab","ba","bab","abb"]],"expected":true},{"args":["",["a","aa","ab","ba","bab","abb"]],"expected":false}],"solution":{"explanation":"<p>Plain recursion re-solves the same suffix exponentially often (\"aaaa\u2026ab\"). The DP over prefix lengths solves each once. Bounding the inner loop by the longest word length turns O(n\u00b2) into O(nL). The input \"a\"\u00d7200 + \"b\" is the one that kills un-memoised backtracking.</p>","python":"def word_break(s, words):\n    ws = set(words); L = max(map(len, ws)); n = len(s); dp = [True] + [False] * n\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        for l in range(1, min(L, i) + 1):\n            if dp[i - l] and s[i - l:i] in ws: dp[i] = True; break\n    return dp[n]\n","cpp":"bool wordBreak(string s, vector<string>& words) {\n    unordered_set<string> ws(words.begin(), words.end()); int L = 0; for (auto& w : words) L = max(L, (int)w.size());\n    int n = s.size(); vector<char> dp(n + 1, 0); dp[0] = 1;\n    for (int i = 1; i <= n; i++) for (int l = 1; l <= min(L, i) && !dp[i]; l++) if (dp[i - l] && ws.count(s.substr(i - l, l))) dp[i] = 1;\n    return dp[n];\n}\n"}}